  "notes": "Measured off N827SY's right side (2025, flipped nose-left) fitted to shapes/B738.json. On the right side the title runs from x 0.149 to 0.437 (5.7 to 16.6 m back), baseline 0.325, caps 0.23; drawn over the same stretch on the left (no open left-side photo found). The fin's orange field: from the leading edge 0.34 to 0.89 of the height, its top arc to the trailing edge at 0.77, down the trailing edge to the root, its lower arc reaching the root about 0.8 of the chord back; the sun centered at fin (0.58, 0.44), 0.84 of the fin's height across its rays. The stripe is blue-2001's (measured on N821SY) and agrees here within the fit. The blue is deeper than the 2001 scheme's royal blue in every photo of the two side by side. Not drawn: the registration and 'BOEING 737-800'. First on the 737-700 N711SY; the 737-700s are gone, so no 737-700 paint is drawn.",
  "history": "Sun Country's 2001 scheme (blue-2001) simplified in December 2016, on 737s joining or repainted until the 2018 livery (standard) replaced it. The 737-8F2s N825SY-N829SY all wore it. A few still do in 2026."
